 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? Roughly break it down with a hatchet before you start a small pit in the middle. Then build up around it. Yes, they work well and are easy to find. Fill them up about halfway and keep them in your pocket as you cut. A small fire pot or tiny stove can heat up quite a lot of water, so don't skimp on it. Put it out completely before you turn in. Pick a spot and walk away from it, putting it out as you go.",
